      "conclusion": "Supported as the established Malaysian Malay term for smartphone by Dewan Bahasa dan Pustaka and Malaysian government usage.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://prpmv1.dbp.gov.my/Search.aspx?d=10&k=telefon+pintar",
        "https://www.mkn.gov.my/web/ms/2024/04/21/pintarkah-kita/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "National split and shared synonym",
      "conclusion": "The split is materially defensible. Smartphone is a shared accepted borrowing/synonym, but the localized preferred forms remain distinct: Indonesian ponsel pintar versus Malaysian Malay telefon pintar. The overlap should be understood as synonym preference, not as identity of the primary localized answers.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
